{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1260484-first-attempt-at-binding-a-paperback","id":1260484,"title":"First attempt at binding a paperback","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-13T23:04:33-07:00","id":1260484,"title":"First attempt at binding a paperback","content":"I've purchased 114 digital supplements on Drive Thru RPG to date and wanted to try to create dead tree copies from the PDFs. 3 ring binders look ugly This was my go at making a paperback.<br /> <br /> I'm apparently not allowed to make attachments, so here's what it looked like:<br /> <br /> &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ma2i1haf1568bs6/MVIMG_20181014_013604_2-COLLAGE.jpg?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">A link to what the paperback looks like</a>&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;<br /> <br /> My method was simple:<br /> 1) Print out all sheets<br /> 2) Trim left edge to remove white gutter<br /> 3) Clamp together pages (I used two metal rulers and a pair of hand clamps)<br /> 4) Glue (I used bookbinder's glue which is just the expensive version of Elmer's glue)<br /> 5) Create spine as supplements don't include these (I used the template pack from DTRPG for v20 plus Mr. Gone's font pack, I played around to get the right width)<br /> 6) Laminate cover (I used an 11 x 17 lamination pouch laid out with back cover, spine, front cover)<br /> 7) Mark where spine will go<br /> 8) Hot glue that area<br /> 9) press inner pages into glue, hold for a few seconds until hot glue cools<br /> 10) bend cover appropriately<br /> <br /> And I got the above.<br /> <br /> Things I need to work on.<br /> -Page registration, my paper cutter is slightly off square<br /> -The cover, I think 11 x 17 100 lb paper will do better but it'll be tricky to print onto<br /> -Full gluing, if the glue doesn't completely cover all pages you'll have a weak spot<br /> <br /> Next I'm going to try a cloth hardcover binding of Beckett's Jyhad Diary<br /> <br /> And before you think this is a clever ploy for me to sell copies of supplements and rake in the duckets, the above took me about 4 hours plus materials cost. This exercise was strictly to see if I could make a paperback and it'd be waaaay cheaper to just buy a POD copy. I plan to eventually make custom hatchet supplements at some point, (copies of text without the fiction pieces and art to have a slimmed down ST copy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-14T09:43:35-07:00","id":1260529,"title":"","content":"well, hats off<br /> I don't think I could do it, but seems coming out pretty nicely","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 